'CONTINUOUS MONITORING':{label:'FOLLOW THE SIGNAL',story:'A patient’s condition changes. The room detects something different. The unit decides whether it matters. The right clinician needs context and a way to respond. The organization needs consistent thresholds and accountability.',aha:'The sensor is the smallest part of the decision. The real design question is whether the whole response chain works.'},
'VIRTUAL CARE':{label:'FOLLOW THE PATIENT',story:'A patient in the room needs a specialist who is somewhere else. The connection must work in the room, fit the bedside team’s workflow, reach the right clinician, carry the right patient context and potentially continue after discharge.',aha:'What looked like a camera in a patient room is actually a care-delivery model spanning the organization.'},
'INTELLIGENT COMMUNICATION':{label:'FOLLOW THE REQUEST',story:'A care need is identified at the bedside. The request must find the right role, reach the person currently responsible, receive acknowledgement and escalate if nobody responds.',aha:'A message is only useful when the entire route from need to response has been designed.'},
'ADAPTABLE CARE':{label:'FOLLOW THE CARE CHANGE',story:'A different patient population, staffing model or equipment set changes how the room is used. The unit adjusts assignments, the facility supports moves and services, and system standards determine what can change without starting over.',aha:'Adaptability is not extra space alone. It is the ability to change care without the building becoming the barrier.'},
